{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/837011-rite-of-the-seed-of-desire","id":837011,"title":"Rite of the Seed of Desire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-25T07:11:01-08:00","id":837011,"title":"Rite of the Seed of Desire","content":"So, a player who's character recently has had some setbacks and who is probably at the bring of Harano (although there was a Rite of Comfort) asked, if this rite could help her character.<br /> <br /> The Rite usually only works on desires, but I guess the desire to suicide or even revenge is not necessarily in the focus of the rite, or is it?<br /> <br /> What do you think, would the Rite be a mean to address problems not related to desires or only loosely related?<br /> Or would leeway in that regard open the rite up to abuse and pretty much make it a universal mental health tool ?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or health period, since it probably can be used for all kinds of addictions - possibly skipping even withdrawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:56:45-08:00","id":837170,"title":"","content":"Well, what sort of setbacks are facing the character in question? What does the character want- are they actively suicidal, or do they simply want to give in to their despair and give up?<br /> <br /> From the rite: &quot;Only those Stargazers who are plagued by grievous desires (or who have already given into them) are the subject of this rite. A Stargazer who is addicted to pain medication (or, alternatively, pain) is a good choice, as is a Stargazer with a dangerous love of money, women, or alcohol.&quot;<br /> <br /> If what the character wants is negative, this might be a good way to mitigate their destructive tendencies. I would argue the temptation to fall into harano might be a desire that could be prevented with this rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:27:49-08:00","id":837339,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't hold that one &quot;desires&quot; suicide. Suicide usually comes from a sense of despair. Utterly different. I wouldn't use this rite.<br /> <br /> If the players is looking for something to help the character move past his failures or problems, then a vision quest of some sort would be more appropriate. Start with some kind of purification ceremony followed by the Rite of Cleansing. Then perform some activity to cause visions - go into a sweat lodge, take some kind of entheogen, perform an ecstatic dance, suffer deprivation, whatever is culturally appropriate. Receive the vision. Then go on a quest into the umbra. Confront the reasons for the character's failures or why he can't overcome his despair at them, and then allow a symbolic victory. Let the player know that the character needs to have learned something and really undergo some character development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:34:04-08:00","id":837421,"title":"","content":"Well, death as a means to end one's own suffering is kind of a desire...<br /> <br /> The characters reason for being at the brink of Harano are the recent deaths of two pack mates and the falling out with the remaining pack mate, who then went on to kill his adoptive sister (who was in another pack in the sept and with whom the character was good friends). So, certainly a series of unfortunate events made her life pretty desolate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}